# .npmrc.example — consumer template for installing @willramdev/* from GitHub Packages.
#
# Copy this file to a .npmrc in your OWN project, then provide a GitHub personal
# access token (PAT) scoped to `read:packages` ONLY (least privilege — a consumer
# never needs write:packages or repo to install).
#
# Keep the real token OUT of source control: prefer the environment-variable form
# below and export the token in your shell / CI, e.g.
#   export GITHUB_TOKEN=your_read_packages_pat
# npm expands ${GITHUB_TOKEN} at install time, so this committed example never
# embeds a secret. Do NOT commit a real .npmrc that contains a token value.

# Scope -> registry map. This line is the part SHARED with the project's own
# .npmrc; it points every @willramdev package at the GitHub Packages registry.
@willramdev:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# Auth line. This is what makes THIS file the CONSUMER template — it must NOT be
# copied into the project's project-level .npmrc (that file carries only the
# scope->registry map, no auth). Token is supplied via env-var expansion, never
# a literal PAT.
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
